<div id="privacy">
    <div id="privacy-content">
        <div id="p-header">
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <h3>Elite Industrial Services</h3>
            <p>Effective Date: September 7, 2026</p>
        </div>

        <article>
            <p>Elite Industrial Services ("EIS," "we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect through our website, eisdiv.com (the "Site"), how we use it, and the choices you have. By using the Site, you agree to the practices described in this policy.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <h3>Information You Provide to Us</h3>
            <p>When you submit our contact form, we collect the information you enter, which may include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Full name</li>
                <li>Email address</li>
                <li>Company name</li>
                <li>Service type requested (Maintenance, Installation, Repair, or Consultation)</li>
                <li>Project details you provide in the message field</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We use this information only to respond to your inquiry and discuss the services you've requested. We do not currently offer online purchases, user accounts, or any other means of submitting personal information through the Site.</p>

            <h3>Information Collected Automatically</h3>
            <p>We may use website analytics tools, such as Google Analytics, and similar cookie- or pixel-based technologies to understand how visitors use our Site — for example, which pages are viewed, how long visitors stay, and what device or browser they use. This information is generally collected in aggregate and is not used to personally identify you. Where we implement analytics, the provider's own privacy policy will govern how they process this data (for Google Analytics, see policies.google.com/privacy).</p>
            <p>Our web server may also automatically log standard technical information, such as your IP address, browser type, and the date and time of your visit, for security and site-performance purposes</p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>2. Cookies</h2>
            <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device. If and when analytics tools are added to this Site, they may use cookies to collect the usage information described above. You can control or disable cookies through your browser settings; note that some Site features may not function properly if cookies are disabled.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Respond to inquiries submitted through our contact form</li>
                <li>Provide quotes, schedule consultations, and deliver the services you request</li>
                <li>Maintain and improve the Site and our services</li>
                <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>

                <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties for their own marketing purposes.</p>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>4. How We Share Information</h2>
            <p>We may share information with:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Service providers who help us operate the Site or our business (such as our web host, email provider, and, if implemented, analytics providers), who are only permitted to use it to provide services to us</li>

                <li>Legal and safety purposes, if required to comply with a law, regulation, subpoena, or legal process, or to protect the rights, property, or safety of EIS, our customers, or others</li>

                <li>Business transfers, if EIS is involved in a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, in which case information may be transferred as part of that transaction</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
            <p>We retain information submitted through our contact form for as long as needed to respond to your inquiry and for a reasonable period afterward for our business records, unless you ask us to delete it sooner (see Section 7).</p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
            <p>We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards to protect the information we collect. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>7. Your Choices</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Contact form data: You may request that we delete personal information you submitted through our contact form by emailing us at the address below</li>
                <li>Marketing communications: If we ever send you marketing emails, you may opt out by following the unsubscribe instructions in that email or by contacting us directly.</li>
                <li>Cookies: You can manage cookie preferences through your browser settings.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>8. Third-Party Links</h2>
            <p>Our Site may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of those sites, and we encourage you to review their privacy policies before providing any information.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>Our Site is intended for business and general audiences and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or for legal or operational reasons. The "Effective Date" above indicates when this policy was last revised. Material changes will be posted on this page.</p>
        </article>
        
        <article>
            <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
            <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or would like to exercise any of the choices described above, please contact us:</p>
